estion-capture/14040368/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ce348c1bc77296bc452234ff6c991750cf0935398311059dab98c49f2daed34" "basis" 1431 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040368/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24575" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=7(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+1)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040368/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ce348c1bc77296bc452234ff6c991750cf0935398311059dab98c49f2daed34" "basis" 1431 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040368/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-24575" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040368/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ce348c1bc77296bc452234ff6c991750cf0935398311059dab98c49f2daed34" "basis" 1431 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040368/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "381c04cd393228257fa31997325a0e5efb63c014f4b4d933753c0315c1e3a20c" "basis" 1923 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=x \\\\ y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t & =1 \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡t & =1-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe used here that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t>0$ in the range $0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nNow, using the definition of a tangent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{\\sqrt{1-{sin}^{2}⁡t}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=x$ and $\\operatorname{tan}⁡t=y$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "381c04cd393228257fa31997325a0e5efb63c014f4b4d933753c0315c1e3a20c" "basis" 1923 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15759" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "434bbc310bcc9fbc66abd7f8aa19f2097f08edade4492c2adb9bc6c8895259d7" "basis" 1923 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-15759" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060376/state.json" "file_sha256" "381c04cd393228257fa31997325a0e5efb63c014f4b4d933753c0315c1e3a20c" "basis" 19